# Every path requires @iamwatchdogs as an owner.
#
# The first non-comment line must be this whole-repo wildcard: a narrower first
# line leaves the remaining paths with no required reviewer, and CODEOWNERS is
# evaluated top-down.
* @iamwatchdogs

# The owners file gates itself, so an attacker cannot quietly reassign review.
.github/CODEOWNERS @iamwatchdogs

# Release and CI plumbing are the files where a wrong change is invisible until
# something ships. Keeping them owned explicitly is belt-and-braces with the
# wildcard above, and documents the intent for whoever reads this next.
/.github/workflows/ @iamwatchdogs
